Summary: Don't overrun the stack opening a database by a path without a backslash
Category: apps
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: dlls/msi/database.c (MSI_OpenDatabaseW); written for wine-mac-builds.
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: MSI_OpenDatabaseW takes a path with no backslash as relative to the
 current directory and built "<current directory>\<path>" with lstrcatW in
 a MAX_PATH buffer on the stack, with no length check. A Unix path, which
 Wine accepts anywhere a file name goes, has no backslash, so a long one
 opened from a deep current directory ran past the buffer and overwrote
 the caller's locals or return address with path text. db->path is now
 allocated at the length it needs; what it holds is unchanged.
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine) ran msiexec /i with the
 package's Mac path (203 characters, /var/folders/.../Setup.msi): Waverly
 Academy's disc install crashed within half a second, 3 of 3 times, under
 the console account and not in Screen Slots slots (whose processes start
 in a shorter directory). The fault varied with the stack layout: CopyFileW
 handed path text as its source, or a jump to path text. Second Chance
 now passes the package's Windows path instead.
Uncertain: The path held for a Unix name stays "<current directory>\<Unix
 path>", as before; nothing found uses it to open the file again.
Evidence: On an APFS clone of Second Chance's build and prefix (host14
 tree, macOS 26.7.2), with Setup.msi also 203 characters away: from a
 117-character current directory msiexec crashed on host14 (1 run), and
 from / it opened the package (1 run). With this change, from the same
 117-character directory, the install ran to InstallFinalize and exited 0
 (1 run).
Applies to: wine 10.0 (macfixes, after 0071)
Status: 2026-11-22 (evening): in a local test build (macfixes-10.0-build0,
 not published): msi-unix-path passes (i686 and x86_64, 1 run each).
 2026-11-22: ported from 11.22 (applies unchanged); not yet in a build.
 msi-unix-path crashes on macfixes-10.0-build7 (i686 and x86_64,
 exit code 5; 1 run each), as on 11.22 before this patch.

diff --git a/dlls/msi/database.c b/dlls/msi/database.c
--- a/dlls/msi/database.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/database.c
@@ -148,7 +148,6 @@
     UINT mode;
     STATSTG stat;
     BOOL created = FALSE, patch = FALSE;
-    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
 
     TRACE("%s %s\n",debugstr_w(szDBPath),debugstr_w(szPersist) );
 
@@ -256,14 +255,19 @@
 
     if (!wcschr( save_path, '\\' ))
     {
-        GetCurrentDirectoryW( MAX_PATH, path );
-        lstrcatW( path, L"\\" );
-        lstrcatW( path, save_path );
+        /* Taken as relative to the current directory. A Unix path has no
+         * backslash either, so the result can be longer than MAX_PATH. */
+        DWORD len = GetCurrentDirectoryW( 0, NULL ) + 1 + lstrlenW( save_path );
+
+        if ((db->path = malloc( len * sizeof(WCHAR) )))
+        {
+            GetCurrentDirectoryW( len, db->path );
+            lstrcatW( db->path, L"\\" );
+            lstrcatW( db->path, save_path );
+        }
     }
     else
-        lstrcpyW( path, save_path );
-
-    db->path = wcsdup( path );
+        db->path = wcsdup( save_path );
     db->media_transform_offset = MSI_INITIAL_MEDIA_TRANSFORM_OFFSET;
     db->media_transform_disk_id = MSI_INITIAL_MEDIA_TRANSFORM_DISKID;
 
